IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc7-s183-base`
IMPORT `ccc7-s183-definitions`

-- ccc7-s184-applications.l4 -- sections 184.2 (interception with consent: the application, the judge, the authorization) and 184.3 (applications by telecommunication) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part VI.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against it.
-- What these sections mean to the person in the seat: whether an interception made with the consent of one party, with a judge's authorization, is lawful (it is a saving limb of section 184(2)(b)); what the judge had to be told and could not
-- authorize; and how long such an authorization may last. Facts are plain inputs; defined terms of other sections are MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs named for the section.
-- Grants named "may" with an "if" gate answer NOTHING when the gate fails (ruling of 2026-11-12). A requirement ("shall") that is not met answers JUST FALSE (the provision's own question).

§ `Section 184.2 -- Interception with consent`

-- 184.2(1): "A person may intercept, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, a private communication where either the originator ... or the person intended by the originator to receive it has consented
-- to the interception and an authorization has been obtained pursuant to subsection (3)." A "may ... where" grant: a failed "where" is JUST FALSE under the guide's ruling (b), listed for a lawyer in the fork register (F11, count in NOTES.md), not decided here.
-- src:3782 | Interception with consent
-- src:3783 | 184.2 (1) A person may intercept, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, a private communication where either the originator of the private communication or the person intended by the originator to receive it has consented to the interception and an authorization has been obtained pursuant to subsection (3).
@ref Criminal Code s 184.2(1) (src:3782-3783)
GIVEN `the interception is by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the communication is a private communication, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `either the originator or the person intended by the originator to receive it has consented to the interception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an authorization has been obtained pursuant to subsection (3), by s 184.2(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.2(1) a person may intercept a private communication with the consent of a party and an authorization` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`either the originator or the person intended by the originator to receive it has consented to the interception` AND `an authorization has been obtained pursuant to subsection (3), by s 184.2(3)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where either the originator of the private communication or the person intended by the originator to receive it has consented to the interception and an authorization has been obtained pursuant to subsection (3)"
        IF `s 183 three-valued all of` (LIST `the interception is by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183`, `the communication is a private communication, by s 183`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the thing is a device or the communication a private communication is for section 183 and is not covered

DECLARE `s 184.2(2) judge applied to` IS ONE OF
    `s 184.2(2) a provincial court judge`
    `s 184.2(2) a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
    `s 184.2(2) a judge as defined in section 552`
    `s 184.2(2) a judge of none of those kinds`

-- 184.2(2): "An application for an authorization under this section shall be made by a peace officer, or a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce any federal or provincial law and whose duties include
-- the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament, ex parte and in writing to a provincial court judge, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552, and shall be accompanied by an affidavit ...
-- deposing to the following matters: (a) ... (e)." The function says whether the application meets the subsection: JUST TRUE if every requirement is met, JUST FALSE if one is not ("shall").
-- src:3784 | Application for authorization
-- src:3785 | (2) An application for an authorization under this section shall be made by a peace officer, or a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce any federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament, ex parte and in writing to a provincial court judge, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552, and shall be accompanied by an affidavit, which may be sworn on the information and belief of that peace officer or public officer or of any other peace officer or public officer, deposing to the following matters:
-- src:3786 | (a) that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this or any other Act of Parliament has been or will be committed;
-- src:3787 | (b) the particulars of the offence;
-- src:3788 | (c) the name of the person who has consented to the interception;
-- src:3789 | (d) the period for which the authorization is requested; and
-- src:3790 | (e) in the case of an application for an authorization where an authorization has previously been granted under this section or section 186, the particulars of the authorization.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.2(2) (src:3784-3790)
GIVEN `the applicant is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a public officer, by s 2 public officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the public officer has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce any federal or provincial law and their duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made ex parte` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      judge IS A `s 184.2(2) judge applied to`
      `the application is accompanied by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this or any other Act of Parliament has been or will be committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the particulars of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the name of the person who has consented to the interception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the period for which the authorization is requested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an authorization has previously been granted under this section or section 186` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the particulars of that authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.2(2) the application meets the requirements of the subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the requirements` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the requirements` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application for an authorization under this section shall be made by a peace officer, or a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce any federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament, ex parte and in writing"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): whether the applicant is a peace officer or a public officer is for section 2, whose definitions say "includes" and are not covered
    WHERE
        `the requirements` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued all of`
                (LIST `the applicant`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the application is made ex parte`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the application is made in writing`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` (NOT (judge EQUALS `s 184.2(2) a judge of none of those kinds`))
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` (`the application is accompanied by an affidavit` AND `the affidavit deposes that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this or any other Act of Parliament has been or will be committed` AND `the affidavit deposes to the particulars of the offence` AND `the affidavit deposes to the name of the person who has consented to the interception` AND `the affidavit deposes to the period for which the authorization is requested`)
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` ((NOT `an authorization has previously been granted under this section or section 186`) OR `the affidavit deposes to the particulars of that authorization`))
        `the applicant` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued any of`
                (LIST `the applicant is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer`
                    , `s 183 three-valued all of` (LIST `the applicant is a public officer, by s 2 public officer`, `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the public officer has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce any federal or provincial law and their duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament`))

-- 184.2(2) (the affidavit "which may be sworn on the information and belief of that peace officer or public officer or of any other peace officer or public officer"): a permission about whose belief the affidavit rests on.
-- src:3785 | (2) An application for an authorization under this section shall be made by a peace officer, or a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce any federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament, ex parte and in writing to a provincial court judge, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552, and shall be accompanied by an affidavit, which may be sworn on the information and belief of that peace officer or public officer or of any other peace officer or public officer, deposing to the following matters:
@ref Criminal Code s 184.2(2) (src:3785-3785)
GIVEN `the affidavit is sworn on the information and belief of that peace officer or public officer or of any other peace officer or public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.2(2) the affidavit may be sworn on information and belief` MEANS
    IF `the affidavit is sworn on the information and belief of that peace officer or public officer or of any other peace officer or public officer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which may be sworn on the information and belief of that peace officer or public officer or of any other peace officer or public officer"

-- 184.2(3): "An authorization may be given under this section if the judge to whom the application is made is satisfied that (a) there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this or any other Act of Parliament has been or will be committed;
-- (b) either the originator ... or the person intended ... has consented to the interception; and (c) there are reasonable grounds to believe that information concerning the offence referred to in paragraph (a) will be obtained through the interception sought."
-- A grant ("may be given") with an "if" gate: a failed gate is NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12; fork F8).
-- src:3791 | Judge to be satisfied
-- src:3792 | (3) An authorization may be given under this section if the judge to whom the application is made is satisfied that
-- src:3793 | (a) there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this or any other Act of Parliament has been or will be committed;
-- src:3794 | (b) either the originator of the private communication or the person intended by the originator to receive it has consented to the interception; and
-- src:3795 | (c) there are reasonable grounds to believe that information concerning the offence referred to in paragraph (a) will be obtained through the interception sought.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.2(3) (src:3791-3795)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this or any other Act of Parliament has been or will be committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that either the originator or the person intended by the originator to receive it has consented to the interception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that information concerning the offence will be obtained through the interception sought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.2(3) an authorization may be given under section 184.2` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this or any other Act of Parliament has been or will be committed`
       AND `the judge is satisfied that either the originator or the person intended by the originator to receive it has consented to the interception`
       AND `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that information concerning the offence will be obtained through the interception sought`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge to whom the application is made is satisfied that"

-- 184.2(4)(e): "be valid for the period, not exceeding sixty days, set out therein", subject to section 186.1 ("Notwithstanding paragraphs 184.2(4)(e) and 186(4)(e)"), whose answer is an input.
-- Dates, not a day count: the period runs from the day it begins to the day it ends, both counted (a period from 1 March to 29 April is 60 days).
-- src:3796 | Content and limitation of authorization
-- src:3797 | (4) An authorization given under this section shall
-- src:3798 | (a) state the offence in respect of which private communications may be intercepted;
-- src:3799 | (b) state the type of private communication that may be intercepted;
-- src:3800 | (c) state the identity of the persons, if known, whose private communications are to be intercepted, generally describe the place at which private communications may be intercepted, if a general description of that place can be given, and generally describe the manner of interception that may be used;
-- src:3801 | (d) contain the terms and conditions that the judge considers advisable in the public interest; and
-- src:3802 | (e) be valid for the period, not exceeding sixty days, set out therein.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.2(4) (src:3796-3802)
GIVEN `the day the period begins` IS A DATE
      `the day the period ends` IS A DATE
      `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.2(4)(e) the period of the authorization is within the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (Day `the day the period ends` MINUS Day `the day the period begins`) PLUS 1 AT MOST 60
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 186.1 lets the period exceed sixty days is for that section and is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "be valid for the period, not exceeding sixty days, set out therein"

-- 184.2(4): "An authorization given under this section shall (a) state the offence in respect of which private communications may be intercepted; (b) state the type of private communication that may be intercepted;
-- (c) state the identity of the persons, if known, whose private communications are to be intercepted, generally describe the place ..., and generally describe the manner of interception that may be used;
-- (d) contain the terms and conditions that the judge considers advisable in the public interest; and (e) be valid for the period, not exceeding sixty days, set out therein."
-- src:3796 | Content and limitation of authorization
-- src:3797 | (4) An authorization given under this section shall
-- src:3798 | (a) state the offence in respect of which private communications may be intercepted;
-- src:3799 | (b) state the type of private communication that may be intercepted;
-- src:3800 | (c) state the identity of the persons, if known, whose private communications are to be intercepted, generally describe the place at which private communications may be intercepted, if a general description of that place can be given, and generally describe the manner of interception that may be used;
-- src:3801 | (d) contain the terms and conditions that the judge considers advisable in the public interest; and
-- src:3802 | (e) be valid for the period, not exceeding sixty days, set out therein.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.2(4) (src:3796-3802)
GIVEN `the authorization states the offence in respect of which private communications may be intercepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorization states the type of private communication that may be intercepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorization states the identity of the persons, if known, whose private communications are to be intercepted, generally describes the place and generally describes the manner of interception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorization contains the terms and conditions that the judge considers advisable in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 184.2(4)(e)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.2(4) the authorization has the content the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the authorization states the offence in respect of which private communications may be intercepted` AND `the authorization states the type of private communication that may be intercepted` AND `the authorization states the identity of the persons, if known, whose private communications are to be intercepted, generally describes the place and generally describes the manner of interception` AND `the authorization contains the terms and conditions that the judge considers advisable in the public interest`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An authorization given under this section shall"
        OTHERWISE `s 184.2(4)(e)`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE ("not exceeding sixty days"); NOTHING when section 186.1 is not covered

-- 184.2(5): "A judge who gives an authorization under this section may, at the same time, issue a warrant or make an order under any of sections 487, 487.01, 487.014 to 487.018, 487.02, 492.1 and 492.2 if the judge is of the opinion that
-- the requested warrant or order is related to the execution of the authorization." The list of sections is not closed with "only"; an "if" gate. The same list is repeated in 186(8) and 188(6): the helper below is used by those too.
-- Section numbers are decimals: "487.014 to 487.018" includes 487.015 to 487.017.
-- src:3803 | Related warrant or order
-- src:3804 | (5) A judge who gives an authorization under this section may, at the same time, issue a warrant or make an order under any of sections 487, 487.01, 487.014 to 487.018, 487.02, 492.1 and 492.2 if the judge is of the opinion that the requested warrant or order is related to the execution of the authorization.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.2(5) (src:3803-3804)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 184.2(5) the section is one of those the subsection lists` MEANS
        (provision's `section` EQUALS 487)
    OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 487.01)
    OR ((provision's `section` AT LEAST 487.014) AND (provision's `section` AT MOST 487.018))
    OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 487.02)
    OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 492.1)
    OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 492.2)

-- src:3803 | Related warrant or order
-- src:3804 | (5) A judge who gives an authorization under this section may, at the same time, issue a warrant or make an order under any of sections 487, 487.01, 487.014 to 487.018, 487.02, 492.1 and 492.2 if the judge is of the opinion that the requested warrant or order is related to the execution of the authorization.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.2(5) (src:3803-3804)
GIVEN `the warrant or order requested` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the judge gives the authorization under section 184.2 and acts at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that the requested warrant or order is related to the execution of the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.2(5) the judge may at the same time issue the related warrant or make the related order` MEANS
    IF `s 184.2(5) the section is one of those the subsection lists` `the warrant or order requested`
       AND `the judge gives the authorization under section 184.2 and acts at the same time`
       AND `the judge is of the opinion that the requested warrant or order is related to the execution of the authorization`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sections the subsection lists are not said to be the only ones, and a failed "if" gate on a grant is not a "may not"

§ `Section 184.3 -- Applications by telecommunication`

DECLARE `s 184.3(1) kind of application` IS ONE OF
    `s 184.3(1) an application for an authorization under subsection 184.2(2)`
    `s 184.3(1) an application for an authorization under subsection 185(1)`
    `s 184.3(1) an application for an authorization under subsection 186(5.2)`
    `s 184.3(1) an application for an authorization under subsection 188(1)`
    `s 184.3(1) an application for an extension under subsection 185(2)`
    `s 184.3(1) an application for an extension under subsection 196(2)`
    `s 184.3(1) an application for an extension under subsection 196.1(2)`
    `s 184.3(1) an application to renew an authorization under subsection 186(6)`
    `s 184.3(1) an application of another kind`

-- 184.3(1): "A person who is permitted to make one of the following applications may submit their application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing: (a) an application for an authorization under subsection 184.2(2), 185(1), 186(5.2)
-- or 188(1); (b) an application for an extension under subsection 185(2), 196(2) or 196.1(2); (c) an application to renew an authorization under subsection 186(6)." The list of applications is not closed.
-- src:3805 | Application — telecommunication producing writing
-- src:3806 | 184.3 (1) A person who is permitted to make one of the following applications may submit their application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing:
-- src:3807 | (a) an application for an authorization under subsection 184.2(2), 185(1), 186(5.2) or 188(1);
-- src:3808 | (b) an application for an extension under subsection 185(2), 196(2) or 196.1(2);
-- src:3809 | (c) an application to renew an authorization under subsection 186(6).
@ref Criminal Code s 184.3(1) (src:3805-3809)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 184.3(1) kind of application`
      `the person is permitted to make that application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.3(1) the person may submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` MEANS
    IF (NOT (kind EQUALS `s 184.3(1) an application of another kind`)) AND `the person is permitted to make that application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is permitted to make one of the following applications"

-- 184.3(2): "A judge who receives an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing shall, immediately on the determination of the application, cause it to be placed and sealed in the packet referred to in subsection 187(1)."
-- src:3810 | Sealing
-- src:3811 | (2) A judge who receives an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing shall, immediately on the determination of the application, cause it to be placed and sealed in the packet referred to in subsection 187(1).
@ref Criminal Code s 184.3(2) (src:3810-3811)
GIVEN `the judge received an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.3(2) the judge is bound to cause the application to be placed and sealed in the packet` MEANS
    IF `the judge received an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judge who receives an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing"

-- 184.3(3): "Despite anything in section 184.2 or 188, a person who is permitted to make an application for an authorization under subsection 184.2(2) or 188(1) may submit their application by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing
-- if it would be impracticable in the circumstances to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing." A grant with an "if" gate: NOTHING when it fails.
-- src:3812 | Application — telecommunication not producing writing
-- src:3813 | (3) Despite anything in section 184.2 or 188, a person who is permitted to make an application for an authorization under subsection 184.2(2) or 188(1) may submit their application by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing if it would be impracticable in the circumstances to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.3(3) (src:3812-3813)
GIVEN `the person is permitted to make an application for an authorization under subsection 184.2(2) or 188(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it would be impracticable in the circumstances to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.3(3) the person may submit the application by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing` MEANS
    IF `the person is permitted to make an application for an authorization under subsection 184.2(2) or 188(1)` AND `it would be impracticable in the circumstances to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it would be impracticable in the circumstances to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing"

-- 184.3(4): "An application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing shall include a statement of the circumstances that make it impracticable to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing."
-- src:3814 | Statement of circumstances
-- src:3815 | (4) An application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing shall include a statement of the circumstances that make it impracticable to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.3(4) (src:3814-3815)
GIVEN `the application was submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it includes a statement of the circumstances that make it impracticable to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.3(4) the application includes the statement of circumstances the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application was submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing"
        IF `it includes a statement of the circumstances that make it impracticable to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall include a statement of the circumstances that make it impracticable to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing"

-- 184.3(5): "Any oath required in connection with an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing may be administered by a means of telecommunication."
-- src:3816 | Oath
-- src:3817 | (5) Any oath required in connection with an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing may be administered by a means of telecommunication.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.3(5) (src:3816-3817)
GIVEN `an oath is required in connection with an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.3(5) the oath may be administered by a means of telecommunication` MEANS
    IF `an oath is required in connection with an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any oath required in connection with an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing"

-- 184.3(6): "A judge who receives an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing shall record the application verbatim, in writing or otherwise, and shall, immediately on the determination of the application,
-- cause the writing or recording to be placed and sealed in the packet referred to in subsection 187(1), and a recording sealed in a packet shall be treated as if it were a document for the purposes of section 187."
-- src:3818 | Recording and sealing
-- src:3819 | (6) A judge who receives an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing shall record the application verbatim, in writing or otherwise, and shall, immediately on the determination of the application, cause the writing or recording to be placed and sealed in the packet referred to in subsection 187(1), and a recording sealed in a packet shall be treated as if it were a document for the purposes of section 187.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.3(6) (src:3818-3819)
GIVEN `the judge received an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.3(6) the judge is bound to record the application verbatim and cause it to be placed and sealed in the packet` MEANS
    IF `the judge received an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judge who receives an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing"

-- src:3818 | Recording and sealing
-- src:3819 | (6) A judge who receives an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing shall record the application verbatim, in writing or otherwise, and shall, immediately on the determination of the application, cause the writing or recording to be placed and sealed in the packet referred to in subsection 187(1), and a recording sealed in a packet shall be treated as if it were a document for the purposes of section 187.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.3(6) (src:3818-3819)
GIVEN `it is a recording sealed in a packet under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.3(6) a recording sealed in the packet is treated as a document for the purposes of section 187` MEANS
    IF `it is a recording sealed in a packet under this subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a recording sealed in a packet shall be treated as if it were a document for the purposes of section 187"

-- 184.3(7): "If an application is submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing, the judge shall not give the authorization unless he or she is satisfied that the application discloses reasonable grounds for dispensing with
-- its submission by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing." The function is named for the bar: JUST TRUE = the judge shall not give it yet; JUST FALSE = the "unless" is met, or the application is not one the bar speaks to.
-- src:3820 | Limitation
-- src:3821 | (7) If an application is submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing, the judge shall not give the authorization unless he or she is satisfied that the application discloses reasonable grounds for dispensing with its submission by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.3(7) (src:3820-3821)
GIVEN `the application was submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the application discloses reasonable grounds for dispensing with its submission by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.3(7) the judge shall not give the authorization` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application was submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an application is submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing"
        IF `the judge is satisfied that the application discloses reasonable grounds for dispensing with its submission by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he or she is satisfied that the application discloses reasonable grounds for dispensing with its submission by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 184.3(8): "A judge who gives the authorization, extension or renewal may do so by a means of telecommunication, in which case (a) the judge shall complete and sign the document in question, noting on its face the time and date; (b) if the means of
-- telecommunication produces a writing, the judge shall transmit a copy of the document to the applicant by that means; (c) if the means of telecommunication does not produce a writing, the applicant shall, as directed by the judge, transcribe
-- the document, noting on its face the name of the judge as well as the time and date; and (d) the judge shall, immediately after the authorization, extension or renewal is given, cause the document to be placed and sealed in the packet referred to in subsection 187(1)."
-- src:3822 | Giving authorization, etc.
-- src:3823 | (8) A judge who gives the authorization, extension or renewal may do so by a means of telecommunication, in which case
@ref Criminal Code s 184.3(8) (src:3822-3823)
GIVEN `the judge gives an authorization, extension or renewal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.3(8) the judge may give the authorization, extension or renewal by a means of telecommunication` MEANS
    IF `the judge gives an authorization, extension or renewal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judge who gives the authorization, extension or renewal may do so by a means of telecommunication"

-- src:3822 | Giving authorization, etc.
-- src:3823 | (8) A judge who gives the authorization, extension or renewal may do so by a means of telecommunication, in which case
-- src:3824 | (a) the judge shall complete and sign the document in question, noting on its face the time and date;
-- src:3825 | (b) if the means of telecommunication produces a writing, the judge shall transmit a copy of the document to the applicant by that means;
-- src:3826 | (c) if the means of telecommunication does not produce a writing, the applicant shall, as directed by the judge, transcribe the document, noting on its face the name of the judge as well as the time and date; and
-- src:3827 | (d) the judge shall, immediately after the authorization, extension or renewal is given, cause the document to be placed and sealed in the packet referred to in subsection 187(1).
@ref Criminal Code s 184.3(8) (src:3822-3827)
GIVEN `the judge gave it by a means of telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge completed and signed the document, noting on its face the time and date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the means of telecommunication produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge transmitted a copy of the document to the applicant by that means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant transcribed the document as directed by the judge, noting on its face the name of the judge as well as the time and date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge caused the document to be placed and sealed in the packet immediately after it was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.3(8) the steps the subsection requires have been taken` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge gave it by a means of telecommunication`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in which case"
        IF `the judge completed and signed the document, noting on its face the time and date`
           AND (IF `the means of telecommunication produces a writing` THEN `the judge transmitted a copy of the document to the applicant by that means` ELSE `the applicant transcribed the document as directed by the judge, noting on its face the name of the judge as well as the time and date`)
           AND `the judge caused the document to be placed and sealed in the packet immediately after it was given`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the judge shall complete and sign the document in question, noting on its face the time and date"
